CrossBible, native package
==========================

This package holds CrossBible compiled to machine code for one processor and one C library (the name of the file says which: linux-x64, linux-arm64,
linux-arm; with -musl- for the systems that use musl, as Alpine). It needs no .NET runtime. (The generic package, crossbible-<version>-noarch.tar.gz, runs on every
processor, but needs the .NET runtime, version 11 or later.)

Install:

    tar -xzf crossbible-<version>-<runtime>.tar.gz
    cd crossbible-<version>-<runtime>
    sudo ./install.sh              (into /usr/local)
    ./install.sh --user            (into ~/.local, no root needed)
    ./install.sh --prefix /opt/cb  (into another folder)

Remove: the same command with --uninstall (and the same --user or --prefix).

Without installing: ./crossbible/CrossBible.Desktop

It needs, as every desktop program on Linux: X11 (libX11, libICE, libSM), fontconfig and a font, OpenGL (libGL), ICU (libicu), OpenSSL and zlib.
